                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Mokobara or Nasher Miles — which is bigger?</h3>
                                        <p>Both meaningful scale. Different segments (Mokobara premium-aspirational; Nasher Miles broader accessible-premium). Coexist without direct competition.</p>
                                        <h3>Can new luggage brands compete?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes in category / positioning niching (adventure-specific, women's premium, business travel specialty). Category has room.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest luggage D2C lesson?</h3>
